{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.DepthStratifiedWeightRequirements","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DepthStratifiedWeightRequirements","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Field","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DepthWeightReq.phiDiff_eq_zero_of_weights_vanish","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DepthWeightReq.phiDiff_eq_zero_of_weights_vanish","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DepthStratifiedWeightRequirements.lean#L149-L156","doc":"Corollary of the above at the observable level: a stratum on which the\nweights vanish contributes nothing to the binding, so no choice of\ndistinguished knot at that depth can change anything. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DepthWeightReq.phi_eq_zero_of_weights_vanish","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DepthWeightReq.phi_eq_zero_of_weights_vanish","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DepthStratifiedWeightRequirements.lean#L133-L147","doc":"**A weight family vanishing on the stratum makes the functional vacuous.**\nIf `w_λ = 0` for every `λ` in the depth-`k` stratum `s`, then `Φ_k = 0`\nidentically — for *every* braid, so the stratum carries no information at all.\n\nThis is the invariant behind the `y_λ` exclusion: at `SU(N)` the Markov/Ocneanu\nweight is `y_λ ∝ ∏_□ [N + c(□)]_q / [h(□)]_q`, and a `λ` with more than `N` rows\nhas a cell of content `−N`, contributing `[0]_q = 0`\n(`Eightfold.RowCapObstruction`). Depth `k` means `k + 1` rows, so `y_λ = 0`\nthroughout every stratum of depth `≥ N`. At the production `N = 2` that is\nevery stratum from depth 2 up — including the depth-3 chirality channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DepthWeightReq.crossRatio_invariant_of_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DepthWeightReq.crossRatio_invariant_of_eq","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DepthStratifiedWeightRequirements.lean#L125-L131","doc":"**The cross-nucleus metric is unchanged exactly when the two normalisers\nagree.** The `k₁ = k₂` specialisation of `crossRatio_smul` — the positive form\nof the requirement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DepthWeightReq.crossRatio_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DepthWeightReq.crossRatio_smul","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DepthStratifiedWeightRequirements.lean#L110-L123","doc":"**The cross-nucleus metric moves by exactly the ratio of the two\nnormalisers.** With `B₁, B₂` the predictions for two nuclei and `E₁, E₂` their\nexperimental values, the scored cross-nucleus quantity is\n`(B₁/E₁)/(B₂/E₂)`. Rescaling the weights of nucleus `i` by `kᵢ` multiplies it\nby `k₁/k₂`.\n\nSo the requirement is **not** that `Σ_λ w_λ = 1`, but that the normaliser be\nthe *same for every `n`* — `k₁ = k₂` makes the factor `1`. A family whose total\nmass drifts with `n` (`Σ_λ d_q²/[n]_q! = 0.991 / 1.111 / 1.517` at\n`n = 6 / 9 / 12`) fails this, and distorts every cross-nucleus comparison. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DepthWeightReq.phiDiff_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DepthWeightReq.phiDiff_smul","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DepthStratifiedWeightRequirements.lean#L95-L108","doc":"**A λ-independent rescale of the weights rescales the observable.**\n`Φ` is linear in `w`, so `w → k · w` sends `Φ(free) − Φ(atom)` to\n`k · (Φ(free) − Φ(atom))`. Within one nucleus this is a global factor and\ncancels out of any ratio; across nuclei it does not, because `k` is a function\nof `n = 3A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DepthWeightReq.phiDiff_eq_sum_log_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DepthWeightReq.phiDiff_eq_sum_log_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DepthStratifiedWeightRequirements.lean#L77-L93","doc":"**The `d_q` factor inside the logarithm cancels in the observable.**\n`Φ(free) − Φ(atom) = Σ_λ w_λ · log(m_free λ / m_atom λ)`: the common factor\n`c_λ` — here the quantum dimension — contributes nothing, because free and atom\nare summed over the same stratum with the same weights.\n\nConsequence (the reason this is the first lemma): `B` is a `w`-weighted mean of\nlog character-ratios, hence **not a linear functional of the braid element**, so\nit is not a trace and the Markov property is not a requirement on `w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DepthWeightReq.phi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DepthWeightReq.phi","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DepthStratifiedWeightRequirements.lean#L71-L75","doc":"The depth-stratum functional `Φ = Σ_{λ ∈ s} w_λ · log(m_λ · c_λ)`, with\n`m_λ = |χ^λ(β)|` the character magnitude and `c_λ = d_q(λ)` the q-dimension\nfactor the corpus form carries inside the logarithm. ","signatureChunk":0}]}